              "tooltip": "Inner diameter size compensation for normal printing layers. A positive value expands the solid and makes holes smaller; a negative value shrinks the solid and makes holes larger.Caution: If the topological boundaries of the sliced data do not match the original model, an inner diameter may be processed as an outer diameter during compensation.",
